{"id": "clm:87c42f1157d309e596e57f3bedab371897aa1681e111ed6e84602dc75fe4c6e0", "type": "statement", "text": "Studies in different cohorts report that Parkinson's disease subtypes differ in progression: one reports clusters associated with motor progression rates, another reports faster two-year progression in diffuse-malignant patients, and a third reports that data-driven subtypes exhibited the highest progression rates. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6288789/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9937525/", "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13616926/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0152e19726ccd4b2eeda24dd971b8d2408601f02176a389f93f4cd0ae7367021", "ev:1accc8caa1c244233175fad86cd6afc7814b7cbd9a681387d7023deff51aef73", "ev:344c4a563bf33e52a71fe65af672857fff0ea24cee791a8a4f9b31a3e6de1c4a"]}
{"id": "clm:f4caf1fd51ac72ec3e04e1b9d0e8bd310e757bea122365631cb2de4a70f0ba1b", "type": "statement", "text": "The SynNeurGe classification of Parkinson's disease proposes three components, pathological α-synuclein, neurodegeneration defined by neuroimaging and pathogenic gene variants, linked to a clinical component; its authors emphasise initial application exclusively for research, and a European Academy of Neurology page lists it among two recent research frameworks for a biological definition of PD. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38267191/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.ean.org/research/resources/neurology-updates/detail/beyond-the-a-synuclein-seed-amplification-assay-shall-we-re-evaluate-the-biological-definition-of-parkinsons-disease"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:39fea64b72da35daccc5a85438d452ca5a1ccb8edc8b85911250202f073a54fa", "ev:7854e42224e9d1d8c04b7aa2839b051ce55f30d6bfedac9d3a90c2ba80ec412a", "ev:8c5cfdd6291491ce0e6d8f02604f47a83f17bd4a23e13e0ff14d8705b9cb4565", "ev:a1332fcb204402e22ae5a2bfcdbe6f42230eb0afecd352f924f230607dc063f9"]}
{"id": "clm:2ccdbc6a3dab4edbb0dfe30c2f9582f0a09d9233e8f50fcc9417a53b60922946", "type": "statement", "text": "In a preprint, the Global Parkinson's Genetics Program authors report that among 65,509 individuals with Parkinson's disease they identified 9,019 (13.8%) potentially trial-eligible genetic variant carriers, including 6,789 GBA1, 2,084 LRRK2, and 146 dual GBA1-LRRK2 carriers. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13119358/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1709d6996171cbf23d0e0f0a189d1bfc040d5b19d027eec168cf727982f6bfb6", "ev:3a305b43468ce5b33bc98f75d786a2ec27db8895f98e191346cb1c283efd110a"]}
{"id": "clm:15479fabb46b35c0883343f7d199555afc2660579834220c3c2fe00878164e26", "type": "statement", "text": "Two analyses of the PPMI cohort by different author groups report that LRRK2-associated Parkinson's disease includes cases negative on the CSF alpha-synuclein seed amplification assay: one reports 46 negative and 102 positive among 148 LRRK2 parkinsonism cases, and another reports SAA-negative patients were markedly enriched for LRRK2 variants. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11925012/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13116718/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:12acab5fc3eef38b0e9d1330b8f92510851fad7421afe67baa458b92fe8301bf", "ev:30afd1a4562ef86b266eff131dff9ec4bf8f4a21b012f4937236b6363a46e754", "ev:35ecc9fedb81cccc0554a2badd4678f77130a0e87fab31613efdb5b9be9462d0", "ev:49b6c009d224ef9e96b22cc8fa66c038fcb037ba3bb08bde7a9e38b224ea023b", "ev:bd219e633cecdb57aa34fec5996e7dc8011081fd8c62d1c4bab3df7639f3009e", "ev:c2f61d357f03ad191141eaee91716b89bbc60c395e160a19adcbcb53f4387ce2", "ev:d369aa2eaaed0285731cd5a8894eb983bfffb8b8c200390826f3b28e3a495354"]}
{"id": "clm:d0d39390d4b825a9efce987345622046a6643cd88691f0919709e0b4c54d0272", "type": "statement", "text": "Reports differ on motor progression in SAA-negative Parkinson's disease: an analysis of LRRK2 carriers reports less severe motor manifestations and decline without alpha-synuclein aggregates, while a European Academy of Neurology commentary on a PPMI analysis reports faster time to motor disability milestones in SAA-negative PD, with a relatively small sample. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11925012/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.ean.org/research/resources/neurology-updates/detail/beyond-the-a-synuclein-seed-amplification-assay-shall-we-re-evaluate-the-biological-definition-of-parkinsons-disease"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:06ee0d22745e9e1fc04e37974efe790572c51240aba7e172f2394b75c5b3a04c", "ev:77e9e0d280bec277d955bc9277ead56ca56f57721226c6b2230a32d665150490", "ev:e8c2f3f2ad3f30b19643d26803752c5500100e39840be2a435989b07b092e69f"]}
{"id": "clm:eebc5c71a6ad76a5f8ca73c51c54736820a51840ba365b9d1be9be86d20ff6c6", "type": "statement", "text": "The sponsors state that the Phase 2b LUMA study of BIIB122 in early-stage Parkinson's disease did not meet its primary or secondary endpoints (primary endpoint: Time to Confirmed Worsening in the modified MDS-UPDRS Part II and III combined score), and a foundation news article reports that participants treated for at least 48 weeks worsened at a similar rate to placebo. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-05-22)", "source_url": "https://investors.biogen.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biogen-and-denali-therapeutics-provide-update-phase-2b-luma", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.michaeljfox.org/news/news-context-parkinsons-drug-luma-lrrk2-clinical-trial-outcomes"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2052f04a9ce2ed70b742aa5920f74e7fb5dda7a7527085926a9d202a7c82c52b", "ev:8b87527a7f079387c3430008fc4e6002aae837c66baa8a5fec363ec431264cca", "ev:910593b264cf492e6cfb83ba9e962745447ae457f82d53d641451743db5b9d31", "ev:a6ff5e8c9821e7c7909c2da36743f90b7d11f6d26f94285ce914ed0de3f64a1e"]}
{"id": "clm:a09e1f28a1ff91b4c4cf978ae0e05ce8707328a675a7dfa8688d10aac568c6d0", "type": "statement", "text": "The sponsors state that LUMA included individuals with early-stage Parkinson's disease with or without a pathogenic LRRK2 variant, and a foundation news article states that the trial largely included patients without known genetic mutations. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://investors.biogen.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biogen-and-denali-therapeutics-provide-update-phase-2b-luma", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.michaeljfox.org/news/news-context-parkinsons-drug-luma-lrrk2-clinical-trial-outcomes"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:862101750bf70ecc324360e29727092ff922f9c14986f161edf751b949b84514", "ev:caaf733eb650db9577310a2edeb742825f4a5e9a711117b5b3aa9e9e2caad7aa"]}
{"id": "clm:980fb8ad0621f508187482a2cd830bbb6091dacdd11a86452dd45135a069d7cd", "type": "statement", "text": "After LUMA, Biogen and Denali state they will discontinue further development of BIIB122 in idiopathic Parkinson's disease, while Denali continues the Phase 2a BEACON study in carriers of a pathogenic LRRK2 variant. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-05-22)", "source_url": "https://investors.biogen.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biogen-and-denali-therapeutics-provide-update-phase-2b-luma", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.michaeljfox.org/news/news-context-parkinsons-drug-luma-lrrk2-clinical-trial-outcomes"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:01e90bdca5fbbf9ba407744c9fb2fee206cf21de3cc5005a44db065db3045fb5", "ev:1e264679535cefa9330a0e6bb0648833441fa62ecdc7d90a5c0a143a6a5abac7", "ev:616c7f9a49e35cc065402e8527358e37d361f5d6770084dd7eab9b6bccacd8ab", "ev:8b87527a7f079387c3430008fc4e6002aae837c66baa8a5fec363ec431264cca"]}
{"id": "clm:fce3b65eb65f9619d8c9561fa8023a77787a2be4d427b190a01fcad6a1a0a267", "type": "statement", "text": "The registry record lists the Phase 3 LIGHTHOUSE study of BIIB122 in participants with Parkinson's disease and pathogenic LRRK2 variants as TERMINATED, with the stated reason Sponsor Decision. (low confidence) (verified as of 2024-06-26)", "source_url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT05418673", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:471a7597ac1ff82a2c841127131f5676b67875260d90c10de898438b9206e864", "ev:4c8edad73ab4db2e5a12f370d5f221808317c333e41035adb7e8b53be23999fc", "ev:8fd9387b857375607dfbcdb9307d89107d27936df9a5fb44fec4b3d09b4fa7e7"]}
{"id": "clm:504283f9763ff0869132bec9ff69b2b0255cc50fa81a9cae7c9405c2fd48e66c", "type": "statement", "text": "Authors of two papers link the failure of disease-modifying trials in PD in part to heterogeneity, with one noting that negative trials treated all PD patients as a single homogenous group. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7483040/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13616926/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:d3a3e077a5b3a5927f1c0753103356c2581d255c999f4443584255072e22897f", "ev:f18d4199e31419f02e476fca3cc23b0412961ef62ab32bfc6fc5237529639dc1"]}
{"id": "clm:7d652f0c346fb1eeb7e865148e59004f7ca4d1df3406332f4f19d7910795e719", "type": "statement", "text": "The authors of a PPMI-based analysis report that trial power simulations demonstrated that enrolling DM patients could reduce sample size requirements by approximately 50% using standard trial durations compared to unstratified PD cohorts. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13616926/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:16f6a03cd7980e00dfebb940abfe104f740b997119dd65c01566d3829da3b496", "ev:28a533c301fb155e92eb1123499bfc1b37daf5d99574b061a5b8ee3b78138896", "ev:4ccac340c43365efbf942aa8de0aae6484bf57b9abafa8341986301407e6d811"]}
{"id": "clm:b434522ba3716dc3832a1b51a03371bd8455a5e6e6a3e115e469f20691fa8079", "type": "statement", "text": "In a PPMI analysis, the authors report that the diffuse malignant (DM) subtype had the highest GBA1 frequency, 14.0% versus 5.9% in the mild-motor predominant (MMP) subtype. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13116718/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b82b07071394be9f6a4e60cfbca2df6972162a1553b6c2f50b37d1ee65a14e79", "ev:c91222fd4934d19e847bf39b125951087ed6b2679a798668af34226b8a795b8d"]}
{"id": "clm:0a671ae2a565372adf4c1db5396c3826eb83a53d0c6764a26e9ba1f02f1fd1a5", "type": "statement", "text": "Authors report that replication of published PD subtype classifications is limited: a Delphi-panel replication of eight data-driven systems found none reproducible in LABS-PD, and a separate validation study states that replication studies in independent cohorts are currently lacking. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30056038/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PD subtypes and precision medicine"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9937525/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f27ce994e068643549fcbf78b81056f3e4d59b0d98dbedb6aba7ed7b78ad15f9", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:edabd93492c39db7cb79a450b3741a3330c561ee4aca310e3251b84abcb7ede5", "ev:f537b6edc4c0bf23efc896fb70b8f5138e7495d57c96e1ba59ab96c4d0d26ac1"]}
